    "created_at": "2023-05-04T09:14:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-05-04T09:14:22Z",
    "body": "Gecko has \"system event group\", which can be used to implement default handling (as an example) using event listeners.  Listeners in that group are called after the listeners in the default group - there is a separate event propagation for system group, all the listeners in the default group in all the targets are called first.\r\n\r\nBut usually default handling is implemented using internal (c++) PostHandleEvent callback. And there are native callbacks for pre-handling too (needed for example for checkbox). And we have WindowRoot on top of the Window in the event path etc, so there is plenty of flexibility.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
